<concept base="Anywhere" id="t00771">
	<title>Forward Parking Distance Warning</title>
	<conbody>
		<p>Forward Parking Distance Warning will operate when one of the condition is satisfied.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>The gear is shifted from R (Reverse) to D (Drive) with Reverse Parking Distance Warning on</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>The gear is in D (Drive) and the Parking safety button indicator light (<image align="left" href="../../images/WKIA_087.eps" scale="15" placement="inline"/>) is on</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>When shifting the gear to D (Drive) while the function is turned off</p>
				<p>(If <menucascade><uicontrol>Settings</uicontrol><uicontrol>Vehicle</uicontrol><uicontrol>Driver assistance</uicontrol><uicontrol>Parking Safety</uicontrol><uicontrol>Auto PDW (Parking Distance Warning)</uicontrol></menucascade> on the infotainment system selected)</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<note type="note">
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p>Forward Parking Distance Warning operates only when the vehicle speed is 10 km/h (6 mph) or lower.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>If Auto on for Parking Distance Warning is not selected, the Forward Parking Distance Warning function will turn off when the vehicle speed exceeds 30 km/h (18 mph) (indicator on the button turns off).</p>
					<p>The function does not turn back on automatically even if the vehicle slows down to 10 km/h (6 mph) or lower.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>A warning sound will activate when an object is detected within the vehicle’s driving path.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>The warning sound may be turned off while the vehicle is stopped.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</note>
		<section>
			<title>Warning indication and warning sound</title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc" pgwide="true" rowsep="1">
				<tgroup cols="4" colsep="1" outputclass="formatc" rowsep="1">
